hadiths[20]{hadithnumber,text}:
"818","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""For every prophet, there is a supplication for his nation that is accepted. I wish that, if Allah wills, I will postpone my supplication for my nation as intercession for them on the Day of Resurrection."""
"819","From another chain of narration, a similar hadith is narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him."
"820","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever dislikes to meet Allah, Allah dislikes to meet him."" The narrator stated: I came to Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and said to her: If what Abu Hurairah narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) is true, then we are doomed. She said: The one who is doomed is the one who is doomed by the statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Then she said: What does he narrate? I said: He says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever dislikes to meet Allah, Allah dislikes to meet him."" She said: I heard this from him (peace and blessings be upon him), ""Do you know when this will be? This will be when, at the time of death, the gaze is raised, when the breath is constricted in the chest, the fingers are wounded, and the hair stands on end. At that time, whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever dislikes to meet Him, Allah dislikes to meet him."""
"821","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites «لا حول ولا قوة إلا بالله» , it is a cure for ninety-nine diseases for him, the least of which is grief."""
"822","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Every prophet has a supplication that is accepted; when he supplicates, his supplication is granted and whatever he asks for is given to him. As for me, I have reserved my supplication for the intercession of my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection."""
"823","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah is Pure and accepts only that which is pure. Allah has commanded the messengers with what He has commanded the believers. 'O assembly of messengers! Eat of the pure things.' And He said: 'O believers! Eat of the pure things We have provided for you.' Then he mentioned a man who undertakes a long journey, 'his hair is disheveled and his feet are dusty, he raises his hands towards the sky (supplicating), while his food, drink, and clothing are from the unlawful (earnings), and he is nourished from the unlawful, so how can his supplication be accepted?'"""
"824","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Whoever remembers Allah within himself, Allah remembers him within Himself. Whoever remembers Allah in an assembly, Allah remembers him in an assembly better than the one in which he remembered Him. Whoever draws near to Him by a span, He draws near to him by a cubit. Whoever draws near to Him by a cubit, He draws near to him by two arm-lengths. Whoever comes to Him walking, He comes to him running. And whoever comes to Him running, He comes to him at speed."""
"825","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of a treasure from among the treasures of Paradise beneath the Throne? «لا حول ولا قوة إلا بالله» Allah says: My servant embraced Islam and he obeyed Me completely."""
"826","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There are three types of people whose supplication is not rejected: the fasting person until he breaks his fast, the just ruler, and the supplication of the oppressed. Allah raises it above the clouds, and the gates of the heavens are opened for it. Then the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, says: By My Honor! I will surely help you, even if after some time."""
"827","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The supplication of a just ruler is not rejected."""
"828","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “The right of hospitality is three days; whatever is beyond that is charity. And it is not lawful for the guest to stay on after that so as to cause harm to the household.” And I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever supplicates to Allah, He accepts his supplication: either He grants him what he asked for quickly, or He forgives his sins in proportion to his supplication.” Provided he does not supplicate for a sin or for severing ties of kinship, and he does not hasten. It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! How does he hasten? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “He says: I supplicated to my Lord, but He did not accept my supplication, or I am not in need of anything.”"
"829","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah! Forgive my earlier and later sins, my hidden and open slips, and my exceeding the limits which none knows except You. You are the One Who brings forward and You are the One Who puts back. There is no deity except You."""
"830","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) advised Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) towards goodness and said: ""I wish to grant you a few words; be eager for them, ask Allah the Most Merciful for them, and supplicate with them day and night. Say: O Allah! I ask You for faith with well-being, for faith with good character, and for salvation after which there is success and mercy from You, pardon and forgiveness from You, and Your pleasure."""
"831","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Saying Subhan Allah is half of the scale, Allahu Akbar fills the heavens and the earth, and La ilaha illallah reaches its Lord without any veil, covering, or barrier."""
"832","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Allah has chosen for you the best of speech, not from the Qur'an while it is a part of the Qur'an, «لا إله إلا الله، والله أكبر، وسبحان الله وبحمده، والحمد لله رب العالمين، ولا حول ولا قوة إلا بالله العلي العظيم» ."""
"833","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrated from his father, he said: Umm Ayman (may Allah be pleased with her) was the slave woman of the mother of the Prophet Muhammad's (peace be upon him) son Ibrahim. So when she would come, she would say: «السلام لاعليكم» , so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) granted her permission to say only «السلام» ."
"834","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The Greatest Name of Allah is in these two verses «وإلهكم إله واحد لا إله إلا هو الرحمن الرحيم» and in the beginning verse of Surah Al-Imran."""
"835","Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated: Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) went out at the time of ‘Isha and met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took his hand and brought him into the mosque, where a man was supplicating with these words: “O Allah! I ask You, I bear witness that You are Allah, the One, the Only, the Self-Sufficient, Who neither begets nor is begotten, and there is none equal to Him.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “By Him in Whose hand is my soul! He has supplicated to Allah with His Greatest Name; when He is supplicated with it, He responds, and when He is asked with it, He gives.”"
"836","Sayyidah Yasirah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed us: ""You should recite tasbih (SubhanAllah), tahleel (La ilaha illallah), and taqdees (sanctification), and count them on your fingertips, for they will be questioned and they will be made to speak. So do not be heedless, lest you be forgotten from mercy."""
"837","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""There are two supplications that are accepted for the servant: the supplication of the oppressed and the supplication of a Muslim for his (Muslim) brother in his absence."""
